//! Sign-in with external identity providers (`cargo rullst make:oauth`):
//! one module per provider (Google, GitHub, Microsoft, Apple) next to this
//! shared flow.
//!
//! The browser keeps only a random challenge id, in the short-lived
//! `rullst_oauth_challenge` cookie scoped to `/auth/<provider>`. The OAuth
//! state, the PKCE verifier and the OpenID Connect nonce stay in the
//! `rullst_connect_login_challenges` table of the application database
//! (created on first use), and the callback consumes them exactly once.
//!
//! Accounts: a provider identity already linked in `oauth_identities`
//! (provider + the provider's stable subject) signs in. Otherwise the
//! provider must report the email address as verified: a new address creates
//! an account without a password, and an address that already belongs to an
//! account follows `EXISTING_ACCOUNT_POLICY`. Each provider module documents
//! what its subject and email are. Sign-in issues the same `rullst_session`
//! cookie as the password login, carrying the account's session epoch.

pub mod __PROVIDER__;

use crate::controllers::auth_controller::{
    get_csp_nonce, get_csrf_token, normalize_email, utc_timestamp, valid_email,
};
use crate::models::oauth_identity::{self, OAuthIdentity};
use crate::models::user::User;
use crate::pages::auth;
use rullst::auth as rullst_auth;
